20,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems our past successes are tied to shared accessibility, while older blocks hide hazardous materials that cause significant delays.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings show a desperate need for general-purpose rooms, as specialist ones sit idle, and out-of-service rooms are costing us in off-site rentals.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,George,,"The grounds staff are depleted, but interestingly, the bench technicians are spending hours on manual tasks that equipment should handle.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Weather has cost us weeks on exposed work, and projects based on ""comfort"" or ""appeal"" are far more likely to slip their schedules.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Mechanical costs are rising sharply, and we have a worrying lack of reserves for replacing old audiovisual equipment.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, if general rooms are the bottleneck, perhaps a project that creates flexible, bookable space would be most effective.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I agree. The data suggests that versatility is key to avoiding the waste we've seen in specialist areas.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,George,,"@Benjamin, if mechanical costs are rising, we should be careful about any plan requiring heavy ventilation or plant upgrades.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that's a fair point. Also, any outdoor work, like paths, risks the weather delays I've discovered.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, exactly. And we must consider if we can actually afford the maintenance of new high-tech suites without a renewal reserve.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@George, the technicians' manual routines suggest that some existing equipment is failing them. That might be a priority.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Victoria,,But we must balance that against the high demand for general study spaces.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,George,,"True, but if the staff are overwhelmed, a new facility that adds to their burden without relief is a mistake.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we want a project that actually finishes on time, we should avoid ""comfort"" projects and focus on essential infrastructure.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Logic suggests we avoid the high-risk mechanical costs and the weather-dependent outdoor work.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
